WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.879
- When you have that passion,

00:00:01.879 --> 00:00:04.580
you will get back up when
you get knocked down.

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:06.666
All sorts of people say
all sorts of things.

00:00:06.666 --> 00:00:10.267
Yeah, our perspective is
to keep our heads down.

00:00:10.267 --> 00:00:12.501
I feel like the luckiest
person in the world

00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:15.268
every day because of what I get to do.

00:00:15.268 --> 00:00:17.556
You know, I think you have
to believe in yourself.

00:00:17.556 --> 00:00:19.601
I think the minute that
you have a backup plan,

00:00:19.601 --> 00:00:21.527
you've admitted that you're
not going to succeed.

00:00:21.527 --> 00:00:25.783
My journey was one of
jumping in feet-first.

00:00:25.783 --> 00:00:28.258
And there's nothing like
rolling your sleeves up

00:00:28.258 --> 00:00:29.829
and failing a bunch of times to figure out

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:31.095
how to do it right.

00:00:31.095 --> 00:00:33.748
I've always seen money as a tool

00:00:33.748 --> 00:00:36.865
for being able to make a difference.

00:00:36.865 --> 00:00:39.580
Big waves come and they go,
but you're there for a reason.

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:42.045
And the 'saving more lives'
piece, when you're talking

00:00:42.045 --> 00:00:44.735
about someone that you
love, you'd do anything.

00:00:44.735 --> 00:00:47.421
- She's an American
businesswoman and entrepreneur.

00:00:47.421 --> 00:00:50.913
She's the CEO of a blood
test company founded in 2003.

00:00:50.913 --> 00:00:54.731
As of January 2016, Forbes
estimated her net worth

00:00:54.731 --> 00:00:56.761
to be $3.6 billion.

00:00:56.761 --> 00:00:59.820
She's Elizabeth Holmes, and
here are her top 10 rules

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:00.820
for success.

00:01:05.027 --> 00:01:08.218
- I would focus first on why
you're doing what you're doing,

00:01:08.218 --> 00:01:11.925
and really, really understand
if you're building a company,

00:01:11.925 --> 00:01:13.994
what's the reason that
you're building this company,

00:01:13.994 --> 00:01:16.472
and what is the role
that you want to have?

00:01:16.472 --> 00:01:18.243
And why are you there?

00:01:18.243 --> 00:01:19.630
Because once you understand it,

00:01:19.630 --> 00:01:20.869
and you understand your reason for it,

00:01:20.869 --> 00:01:23.090
you'll build the company differently.

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:26.701
I would say to make sure what you're doing

00:01:26.701 --> 00:01:28.947
is something that you love,
and that you are so deeply

00:01:28.947 --> 00:01:32.941
and incredibly passionate
about that if you got fired,

00:01:32.941 --> 00:01:35.225
you would still want to do it.

00:01:35.225 --> 00:01:38.882
And if you weren't CEO, you
would still want to do it,

00:01:38.882 --> 00:01:41.345
because when you have that passion,

00:01:41.345 --> 00:01:44.174
you will get back up when
you get knocked down.

00:01:44.174 --> 00:01:46.022
And you will get knocked
down over, and over,

00:01:46.022 --> 00:01:48.971
and over again, and you
win by getting back up.

00:01:48.971 --> 00:01:52.074
And our journey has been nothing but that,

00:01:52.074 --> 00:01:55.684
in the context of falling
in love with this mission,

00:01:55.684 --> 00:01:57.913
and feeling like the luckiest
people on the planet,

00:01:57.913 --> 00:01:59.849
to be able to do it every single day,

00:01:59.849 --> 00:02:03.114
and fighting for it
because we love it so much.

00:02:03.114 --> 00:02:05.908
And I've always been a great
believer in the concept

00:02:05.908 --> 00:02:07.545
of the 10,000 hour rule.

00:02:07.545 --> 00:02:09.880
When you go so deep in something,

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:12.535
you can become an expert in it,

00:02:12.535 --> 00:02:15.641
and when you love it that
much, you don't let it go.

00:02:15.641 --> 00:02:18.982
And I think that's what winning is about.

00:02:18.982 --> 00:02:21.734
And people, all sorts of
people, say all sorts of things.

00:02:21.734 --> 00:02:25.325
Our perspective is to keep our heads down.

00:02:25.325 --> 00:02:28.211
And we have a very clear mission,

00:02:28.211 --> 00:02:30.691
we know why we're doing this,

00:02:30.691 --> 00:02:33.876
we see every day what this means to people

00:02:33.876 --> 00:02:36.140
in the context of the
ability to afford care,

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:39.640
or not go through what I equate to torture

00:02:43.686 --> 00:02:45.778
in the context of traditional phlebotomy.

00:02:45.778 --> 00:02:47.675
And that's what we focus on,

00:02:47.675 --> 00:02:49.563
and that's all that we focus on,

00:02:49.563 --> 00:02:52.649
because if we can keep doing
that, person by person,

00:02:52.649 --> 00:02:54.941
we will realize this mission.

00:02:54.941 --> 00:02:57.555
- What keeps Elizabeth up
at night, if you sleep?

00:02:57.555 --> 00:02:58.865
(audience laughs)

00:02:58.865 --> 00:03:00.343
And how do you go about tackling that?

00:03:00.343 --> 00:03:02.857
- Well, I don't sleep very much.

00:03:02.857 --> 00:03:04.997
- [Hostess] How many hours do
you get a night on average?

00:03:04.997 --> 00:03:07.557
- I sleep about four hours, yeah.

00:03:07.557 --> 00:03:11.724
I feel like the luckiest
person in the world every day

00:03:14.864 --> 00:03:18.138
because of what I get
to do, and right now,

00:03:18.138 --> 00:03:21.108
building this company is
about building people,

00:03:21.108 --> 00:03:24.554
and really investing in
building the people from within

00:03:24.554 --> 00:03:28.054
our company, so I spend as much of my time

00:03:30.783 --> 00:03:32.466
as humanly possible focusing

00:03:32.466 --> 00:03:35.653
on getting and building the right people,

00:03:35.653 --> 00:03:37.693
because that's how we
realize this mission,

00:03:37.693 --> 00:03:40.140
and how we realize this dream.

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:44.413
So, I don't think I could
be possibly kept up more

00:03:44.413 --> 00:03:46.913
than I already am on that one.

00:03:47.776 --> 00:03:50.262
I mean, the first time that
I went through the process

00:03:50.262 --> 00:03:52.116
of raising money, I assumed
that I was going to have

00:03:52.116 --> 00:03:54.113
to talk to at least 200
people before I found one

00:03:54.113 --> 00:03:56.375
who was going to believe in me,

00:03:56.375 --> 00:03:58.695
so I didn't really care if
people were turning me down,

00:03:58.695 --> 00:04:01.255
because I knew I would
find someone who did.

00:04:01.255 --> 00:04:05.397
- [Woman In Audience] How do
you make people believe in you?

00:04:05.397 --> 00:04:07.708
- How do you make people believe in you?

00:04:07.708 --> 00:04:12.289
You know, I think you have
to believe in yourself.

00:04:12.289 --> 00:04:15.448
And I think you have to have
the conviction in yourself

00:04:15.448 --> 00:04:17.311
to be able to make something happen,

00:04:17.311 --> 00:04:19.487
because ultimately it's up to you,

00:04:19.487 --> 00:04:23.070
and when you have that
level of conviction,

00:04:24.326 --> 00:04:28.306
you'll find that people, or
the resources or the tools

00:04:28.306 --> 00:04:31.044
that you need to make it happen.

00:04:31.044 --> 00:04:33.062
It may take a lot longer than you think,

00:04:33.062 --> 00:04:35.585
but it's about keeping that
conviction in yourself.

00:04:35.585 --> 00:04:37.298
- So did you have a backup plan?

00:04:37.298 --> 00:04:41.465
I mean, if this didn't work
out, what was your alternative?

00:04:42.890 --> 00:04:44.850
Did you have one?

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:48.380
- No, and I think that the
minute that you have a backup

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:50.746
plan, you've admitted that
you're not going to succeed.

00:04:50.746 --> 00:04:54.038
So we are not big on backup plans.

00:04:54.038 --> 00:04:57.705
My journey was one of
jumping in feet-first,

00:04:58.821 --> 00:05:02.929
and so I think if you know
why you're doing something,

00:05:02.929 --> 00:05:06.346
and what it is that you're trying to get,

00:05:07.683 --> 00:05:12.359
then it's a question of being
very, very open to failure.

00:05:12.359 --> 00:05:16.026
And just trying again,
and again, and again,

00:05:18.544 --> 00:05:19.990
until you get it.

00:05:19.990 --> 00:05:23.730
So we codenamed our product,
what started as that patch,

00:05:23.730 --> 00:05:27.730
the Edison because our
premise was we will fail,

00:05:28.622 --> 00:05:31.753
over 1000 times, until we
get this thing to work.

00:05:31.753 --> 00:05:34.398
But we'll get it on the 1001st time.

00:05:34.398 --> 00:05:38.297
And I think that mindset has really guided

00:05:38.297 --> 00:05:39.953
so much of what we've done,

00:05:39.953 --> 00:05:42.844
because there's a
determination to make it work

00:05:42.844 --> 00:05:47.012
no matter what, but you're
not worried about whether

00:05:47.012 --> 00:05:49.654
many of those attempts fail.

00:05:49.654 --> 00:05:51.354
You're embracing it, almost.

00:05:51.354 --> 00:05:53.359
- How have you managed, I mean,

00:05:53.359 --> 00:05:54.710
those are different skill sets,

00:05:54.710 --> 00:05:56.124
founding and running a company.

00:05:56.124 --> 00:05:58.599
How have you developed
each of those skill sets,

00:05:58.599 --> 00:06:01.617
and how have you managed
to lead this company

00:06:01.617 --> 00:06:06.383
from a small organization
to a big startup, still,

00:06:06.383 --> 00:06:08.657
but startup today?

00:06:08.657 --> 00:06:10.766
- Hopefully we'll always be a startup.

00:06:10.766 --> 00:06:14.933
We've had the privilege of,
and I have had the privilege of

00:06:18.382 --> 00:06:22.549
surrounding ourselves with
incredibly smart people,

00:06:25.375 --> 00:06:29.292
and that combined with
jumping in and doing it,

00:06:31.032 --> 00:06:35.199
and teaching myself, is the
way that I've approached

00:06:36.303 --> 00:06:37.891
everything that I've done.

00:06:37.891 --> 00:06:42.264
And there's nothing like
rolling your sleeves up

00:06:42.264 --> 00:06:43.415
and failing a bunch of times

00:06:43.415 --> 00:06:45.230
to figure out how to do it right.

00:06:45.230 --> 00:06:49.147
I've always seen money
as a tool for being able

00:06:50.406 --> 00:06:53.990
to make a difference, and for
us, we reinvest everything

00:06:53.990 --> 00:06:56.730
that we make back into our company.

00:06:56.730 --> 00:06:59.734
And we always will, because
it's about being able

00:06:59.734 --> 00:07:01.591
to create better and better products

00:07:01.591 --> 00:07:03.679
to realize this vision.

00:07:03.679 --> 00:07:07.846
And so I never would have
built the company this way

00:07:10.635 --> 00:07:12.754
if it was about making money.

00:07:12.754 --> 00:07:17.717
It's about creating value,
and money becomes a byproduct

00:07:17.717 --> 00:07:20.413
of being successful and creating value.

00:07:20.413 --> 00:07:24.215
And then it's a tool to
reinvest and to be able

00:07:24.215 --> 00:07:25.506
to continue doing that.

00:07:25.506 --> 00:07:27.628
That's how we think about it.

00:07:27.628 --> 00:07:29.137
I've been knocked down a lot,

00:07:29.137 --> 00:07:33.304
and I became really clear that
this is what I wanted to do.

00:07:35.174 --> 00:07:37.777
And I would start this
company over 10,000 times,

00:07:37.777 --> 00:07:39.054
if I had to.

00:07:39.054 --> 00:07:44.042
And there's been times where
we've invested in people,

00:07:44.042 --> 00:07:46.254
where you build something like this,

00:07:46.254 --> 00:07:50.254
and to me, the people in
our company have always

00:07:52.309 --> 00:07:54.254
been like my family.

00:07:54.254 --> 00:07:56.883
And you make mistakes,
you hire the wrong people,

00:07:56.883 --> 00:07:59.412
and that can be incredibly painful,

00:07:59.412 --> 00:08:02.230
because the damage that
they can do to the company

00:08:02.230 --> 00:08:04.530
is really significant.

00:08:04.530 --> 00:08:08.697
Now, we're under real attack
from the lab industry,

00:08:10.688 --> 00:08:15.341
who is seeding all sorts
of bad stuff about us,

00:08:15.341 --> 00:08:17.741
or false statements about us.

00:08:17.741 --> 00:08:21.574
And we've had to keep
our heads down and focus

00:08:23.236 --> 00:08:24.989
on what we are doing, and the belief that,

00:08:24.989 --> 00:08:29.219
person by person, we will
demonstrate the integrity

00:08:29.219 --> 00:08:30.518
of what we do.

00:08:30.518 --> 00:08:32.979
But I think that clarity of purpose,

00:08:32.979 --> 00:08:34.763
in terms of why we do it,

00:08:34.763 --> 00:08:37.680
makes you capable of weathering it.

00:08:38.635 --> 00:08:40.566
It's kind of like an ocean,
big waves come and they go,

00:08:40.566 --> 00:08:42.934
but you're there for a reason.

00:08:42.934 --> 00:08:46.567
I've always believed that
we're here on this earth

00:08:46.567 --> 00:08:48.321
to try and make a difference in the world,

00:08:48.321 --> 00:08:52.488
and so when I found what I felt
like what I was born to do,

00:08:57.928 --> 00:09:02.263
which was to try and help
contribute to solving a problem

00:09:02.263 --> 00:09:05.013
that I believe, at a human level,

00:09:06.726 --> 00:09:08.821
there's not a lot that matters more.

00:09:08.821 --> 00:09:10.487
- [Host] Access more
dental, save more lives.

00:09:10.487 --> 00:09:12.509
- Yeah, and the saving more lives piece,

00:09:12.509 --> 00:09:14.444
when you're talking about
someone that you love,

00:09:14.444 --> 00:09:16.381
you'd do anything, right?

00:09:16.381 --> 00:09:18.927
And to be able to solve that problem,

00:09:18.927 --> 00:09:20.852
to me, that was the greatest
contribution I could make

00:09:20.852 --> 00:09:22.507
with my life.

00:09:22.507 --> 00:09:23.807
- Thank you guys so much for watching,

00:09:23.807 --> 00:09:25.642
I made this video because
one of you guys asked me to,

00:09:25.642 --> 00:09:27.902
so if there's a famous
entrepreneur that you want

00:09:27.902 --> 00:09:30.522
me to profile next, leave
it in the comments below

00:09:30.522 --> 00:09:32.825
and I will see what I can do.

00:09:32.825 --> 00:09:34.608
I would also love to know which

00:09:34.608 --> 00:09:36.455
of Elizabeth Holmes's top
10 rules hit you the hardest

00:09:36.455 --> 00:09:38.068
or had the biggest impact.

00:09:38.068 --> 00:09:39.620
Leave it in the comments and
we'll join the discussion.

00:09:39.620 --> 00:09:41.615
And one last thing, my
goal with the channel

00:09:41.615 --> 00:09:43.233
is to get it to one million subscribers,

00:09:43.233 --> 00:09:46.638
that's the next goal, so
anything you can do to think of,

00:09:46.638 --> 00:09:49.353
to share the video, tell
friends about it, tweet it,

00:09:49.353 --> 00:09:51.644
add it to playlists, spread
the message a little bit.

00:09:51.644 --> 00:09:53.331
I'd really, really appreciate it.

00:09:53.331 --> 00:09:54.825
Thank you guys so much for watching,

00:09:54.825 --> 00:09:58.325
continue to believe and I'll see you soon.

